  "subdivision_of_building": "The proposals only cover the rear yard area and vault of no.839 High Road and do not include the existing main building itself",
  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Demolition of existing single storey former bank vault and erection of part 2, part 3 and part 4 storey building comprising 7 flats, with integral cycle storage, waste and recycling storage",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its siting, height and massing in close proximity to neighbouring residential properties, would result in significant reductions in daylight and sunlight to neighbouring habitable room windows, the creation of an overbearing sense of enclosure, and unacceptable overlooking from the balconies serving Flats 3 and 5 due to insufficient privacy screening. The development would therefore result in unacceptable harm to the living conditions of existing and future occupiers, particularly those at No. 841 High Road, contrary to Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024) and the design principles of the London Plan (2021) which seek to ensure that development safeguards residential amenity.",
    "In the absence of a completed planning obligation secured through a legal agreement pursuant to Section 106 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, the proposed development fails to secure the planning obligations necessary to mitigate the impacts of the development. The proposal therefore conflicts with Policy 94 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024) and the Waltham Forest Supplementary Planning Document “Planning Obligations” (2017). The required planning obligations include the following (figures applicable at the time of the assessment of the application):A) Highways and Transportation:i) Car Free Development - the development is to be classified as car-free and residents will not be eligible for parking permits.ii) A condition survey is required of the carriageway and footways fronting the site prior to the commencement of any works.iii)&nbsp;A S106 request of £7,000&nbsp;is requested toward improving sustainable modes of transport including walking and cycling in the sites vicinity which will directly benefit new residents in this development.iv) A&nbsp;S106 contribution of £750&nbsp;is requested for CLP monitoring.v) S278 works –Removal of redundant dropped kerb fronting the site.Potential provision of a new dropped kerb for eurobins.Renewal of the footway along the frontage of the site.Renewal of the road markings along the frontage of the site.Possible changes to Controlled Parking Zone bays including changes to Traffic Management Orders and Signage.B) SAMMS:i) SAMMS - A financial contribution of £4,550.00&nbsp;towards Strategic Access Management and Monitoring measures (SAMMs).C) Carbon offset:Carbon Offset Fund (COF) contributions will be required for any shortfall in emission reductions.D) Legal Fees:i) Payment of the Council’s legal fees for the preparation and completion of the Legal Agreement.ii) Monitoring Fee - A financial contribution towards the implementation and monitoring of and securing compliance with the S106, equal to 5% of the total of all other financial contributions ."
  ],
